<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duy Tân</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1900–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Vĩnh San</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duy Tân was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> of the Nguyễn dynasty from 1907 to 1916. Placed on the throne as a child after the French deposed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanh-thai">Thành Thái</a>, he grew opposed to French rule and in 1916 joined a planned uprising by Vietnamese troops. The plot was discovered, and he was deposed and exiled to Réunion; he died in a plane crash in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/duy-tan.jpg" alt="Duy Tân" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duytan_on_throne.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
